<%# locals: bottle
    The bottle's photo in a dark identity band (bottle show, review show).

    PORTRAIT, not square: a bottle is tall, and a square crop of a phone
    snapshot spends most of the frame on the counter behind it.

    It sits directly on the char surface behind a hairline ring, with NO cream
    backing plate. The plate read as a sticker stuck on the dark band, and per
    the design system's de-carding rule it was a second elevated surface the
    masthead didn't need. Same footprint whether there's a photo or the drawn
    placeholder, so two bottles side by side always agree. %>
<div class="shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-oak ring-1 ring-cream/15">
  <% if bottle.display_image %>
    <%= image_tag bottle.display_image.variant(:portrait),
        class: "h-20 w-16 object-cover", alt: bottle.name %>
  <% else %>
    <div class="flex h-20 w-16 items-center justify-center">
      <%= render "bottles/placeholder", bottle: bottle, size: "h-14", tone: :dark %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
